<article class="env-lemma" id="0C43">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0C43">Lemma <span data-tag="0C43">33.40.6</span>.</a> Let $(A, \mathfrak m)$ be a $1$-dimensional reduced Nagata local ring. Then </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \delta \text{-invariant of }A \geq \text{number of geometric branches of }A - 1  \]
</div>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      We may replace $A$ by the strict henselization of $A$ without changing the $\delta $-invariant (Lemma <a href="/tag/0C3W" data-tag="0C3W">33.39.6</a>) and without changing the number of geometric branches of $A$ (this is immediate from the definition, see More on Algebra, Definition <a href="/tag/0C26" data-tag="0C26">15.108.6</a>). Thus we may assume $A$ is strictly henselian and we may apply Lemma <a href="/tag/0C42" data-tag="0C42">33.40.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>